cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AetherNet in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "AetherNet — offline-first mesh networking protocol"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, MIT-licensed mesh networking protocol for offline messaging,
  file transfer, voice, and video over Bluetooth, Wi-Fi Direct, NearLink, LoRa,
  and WebRTC. Implemented byte-for-byte identically in eight programming
  languages (C#, Rust, TypeScript, Python, Go, Kotlin, Swift, C) with
  end-to-end encryption via the Signal Protocol (X3DH + Double Ratchet),
  AODV-style routing, and delay-tolerant store-and-forward.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Geek Network"
    website: "https://thegeek.co.za"
url: "https://github.com/bhengubv/aether-protocol"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bhengubv/aether-protocol"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - mesh-networking
  - offline-first
  - delay-tolerant-networking
  - signal-protocol
  - end-to-end-encryption
  - peer-to-peer
  - bluetooth-low-energy
  - wifi-direct
  - lora
  - webrtc
